# open62541-qnx change: eventloop-ppoll
# SPDX-License-Identifier: MPL-2.0
#
# title: Wait in ppoll() instead of select()
# file: open62541.c
# upstream: arch/eventloop_posix.h arch/eventloop_posix_select.c
# test: highfd.client highfd.sessions robust.idle_client
#
# open62541 waits in epoll on Linux. On every other POSIX system its event
# loop calls select(), and that code puts every registered descriptor into an
# fd_set without comparing it with FD_SETSIZE. A descriptor number of
# FD_SETSIZE or more makes FD_SET() write outside of the fd_set, on the stack
# of UA_EventLoopPOSIX_pollFDs.
#
# The case is within reach wherever FD_SETSIZE is smaller than the number of
# descriptors a process may open (RLIMIT_NOFILE): a server with a few hundred
# connections, or an application that has many files or devices open before
# it starts the server. o6q_envprobe prints both values on the target
# (fd.FD_SETSIZE, fd.rlimit_nofile).
#
# The change keeps the select() code and adds a second version of
# UA_EventLoopPOSIX_pollFDs that waits in ppoll(). It is chosen with
# O6Q_EVENTLOOP_POLL, which is the default on QNX. On Linux the same macro
# replaces epoll, so that the code can be tested there as well.
#
